W: 2. It was in the month of May, my bonnie lassie O,
W: It was in the month of May, my bonnie lassie O,
W: It was in the month of May, when the flowers they were gay,
W: And the lambs did sport and play my bonnie lassie O'
W:
W: 3. Do you mind on yonder hill, my bonnie laddie O,
W: Do you mind on yonder hill, my bonnie laddie O,
W: D'you mind on yonder hill where you swore you would me kill,
W: If you did'na have your will? my bonnie laddie O.
W:
W: 4. Do you mind the banks of Ayre, my bonnie laddie O,
W: Do you mind the banks of Ayre, my bonnie laddie O,
W: Do you mind the banks of Ayre, where you drew me in your snare,
W: And you left me in despair, my bonnie laddie O?
W:
W: 5. O it's you may kill me dead, my bonnie laddie O,
W: O it's you may kill me dead, my bonnie laddie O,
W: O I'll not kill you dead nor make your body bleed,
W: Nor marry you with speed my bonnie lassie O.
W:
W: 6. For the pipes do sweetly play, my bonnie lassie O,
W: For the pipes do sweetly play, my bonnie lassie O,
W: O the pipes do sweetly play and the troops do march away,
W: And it's here I will not stay, my bonnie lassie O.
W:
W: 7. O the shearing's not for you, my bonnie lassie O,
W: O the shearing's not for you, my bonnie lassie O,
W: O the shearing's not for you, for your back it wouldna' bow,
W: And your belly's o'er full, my bonnie lassie O.
